  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are theorems</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are correct<br />For option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is correct<br />For option <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math>,</p><p>When <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> is true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is false then <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is false</p><p>Hence, option <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is incorrect</p>",
